<title>JAPAN: SHIN-ETSU UNIT TO SPEND Y100 BLN FOR WAFERS--PAPER.</title>
<headline>SHIN-ETSU UNIT TO SPEND Y100 BLN FOR WAFERS--PAPER.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shin-Etsu Handotai Co Ltd, a wholly owned subsidiary of Shin-Etsu Chemical Co Ltd, plans to spend 100 billion yen to boost output of high-quality semiconductor silicon wafers by 400 percent from current levels by the end of March 1999, Nihon Keizai Shimbun's wire service said on Friday.</p>
<p>Shin-Etsu Handotai could not immediately confirm the report.  </p>
<p>The unit will invest 50 billion yen in the year to March 31, 1998 and the same amount in the following year on its factories in Japan, Canada and Britain to boost total output to 500,000 wafers a month, the wire service said.</p>
</text>
